                            <title>Missale</title>
                            <note>Graded calendar. Many obits of the Statham family and one of
                                Sachaverell, s. xv. A memorandum by the rector of Morley dated 1441
                                at end of temporale. Secundo folio preterquam.</note>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
                    <history>
                        <origin>
                            <origDate calendar="Gregorian" notBefore="1390" notAfter="1410">s.
                                xiv/xv</origDate>
                        </origin>
                        <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_888">Morley, Derbyshire. Parish
                                church</orgName>
                            <p><q>Dedicacio ecclesie de Morley</q> added early in red at 13
                                July.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">Bought in 1729 by <persName>John
                                Plumptre</persName>, grandson of <persName>Henry
                                Sachaverell</persName> of Morley, <q>with the rest of the family
                                books</q> (fol. iiv). Bookplate of <persName>John
                            Morley</persName>.</provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">The location on the index card is
                            listed as J. H. Plumtre (Little Fredville, Nonington, Kent), on deposit
                            in Canterbury Cathedral since 1966. This is now Canterbury, Cathedral
                            Archives, CCA-U53/1. For further discussion of the book's later
                            provenance, see <bibl>Pete Smith, 'Plumtre House, Nottingham: Colen
                                Campbell and John Plumtre', <title>The Georgian Group
                                    Journal</title> XXX (2022): 37-70 (especially p.
                            54).</bibl></provenance>
                    </history>
